# {{ project_name }}

The **RTT Hello** example logs a message every half second through the debug probe and
blinks the LED on `{{ led_pin }}`. The messages are read by the ST-Link over SWD (RTT) and
decoded on the computer by [defmt](https://defmt.ferrous-systems.com): no UART adapter is
needed.

## Target board

**{{ board_name_en }}** uses the `{{ chip_id }}` microcontroller with
{{ flash_kb }} KB of flash and {{ ram_kb }} KB of RAM. The Rust target is `{{ target_triple }}`.

## Build and see the output

Flash it through an ST-Link: the messages appear in the "RTT" tab. From the command line:

```sh
cargo build --release
probe-rs run --chip {{ probe_rs_name }} target/{{ target_triple }}/release/{{ project_name }}
```

The firmware ELF is written to `target/{{ target_triple }}/release/{{ project_name }}`.

Change `DEFMT_LOG` in `.cargo/config.toml` to see more (`debug`, `trace`) or fewer messages.
